1
00:00:17,929 --> 00:00:21,104
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this is from the Anguttarinika and it's called flies.

2
00:00:24,813 --> 00:00:32,075
[SPEAKER_00]: And the Blessed One says, Bhikkhus, this morning I dressed, took my bowl and robe, and entered Varanasi for alms.

3
00:00:32,455 --> 00:00:48,879
[SPEAKER_00]: While walking for alms, near the cattle-yolking fig tree, I saw a dissatisfied Bhikkhu, seeking gratification outwardly, muddle-minded, confused, without clear comprehension, uncomposed, with a wandering mind and loose sense faculties.

4
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:51,600
[SPEAKER_00]: Hmm.

5
00:01:11,044 --> 00:01:15,345
[SPEAKER_00]: When this was said, a certain bhikkhu asked the Blessed One, what, Bhante, is meant by pollution?

6
00:01:15,965 --> 00:01:17,786
[SPEAKER_00]: What is the stench and what are the flies?

7
00:01:19,786 --> 00:01:24,607
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, longing is what is meant by pollution, polluting yourself.

8
00:01:25,267 --> 00:01:26,328
[SPEAKER_00]: Ill will is the stench.

9
00:01:27,228 --> 00:01:28,988
[SPEAKER_00]: Bad, unwholesome thoughts are flies.

10
00:01:29,808 --> 00:01:36,090
[SPEAKER_00]: It is inevitable that flies will pursue and attack one who has polluted himself and been tainted by a stench.

11
00:01:39,133 --> 00:01:47,515
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you can have these unwholesome thoughts, these repetitive evil thoughts of lust, of ill-will.

12
00:01:47,975 --> 00:01:48,475
[SPEAKER_00]: Why is that?

13
00:01:48,715 --> 00:01:49,976
[SPEAKER_00]: Why are these flies there?

14
00:01:54,277 --> 00:01:55,497
[SPEAKER_01]: So, how do you deal with the flies?

15
00:01:55,557 --> 00:01:57,437
[SPEAKER_01]: You try to kill every fly individually?

16
00:01:58,177 --> 00:02:04,519
[SPEAKER_01]: Preventing the thoughts, dealing with them, antidoting them, managing them, removing them, or remove the reason why they're coming back?

17
00:02:05,695 --> 00:02:08,256
[SPEAKER_01]: ill-will, longing, lust, distraction.

18
00:02:08,397 --> 00:02:10,538
[SPEAKER_01]: Remove that, these thoughts will stop coming.

19
00:02:10,958 --> 00:02:11,738
[SPEAKER_00]: We keep saying that.

20
00:02:11,958 --> 00:02:12,239
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

21
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:14,960
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't want the flies to do that.

22
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:16,081
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's how you abandon them.

23
00:02:16,121 --> 00:02:16,321
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

24
00:02:16,421 --> 00:02:20,243
[SPEAKER_01]: You have flies abandon you by removing that which flies want.

25
00:02:20,983 --> 00:02:21,504
[SPEAKER_01]: The stench.

26
00:02:21,564 --> 00:02:21,844
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

27
00:02:22,004 --> 00:02:27,627
[SPEAKER_01]: And you maintain the stench, you maintain the pollution by acting out, by not being restrained, by not enduring things on the right level.

28
00:02:29,412 --> 00:02:36,341
[SPEAKER_01]: That's exactly how you maintain craving, and longing, and aversion towards pain, and wanting pleasure, all the reasons that these flies keep coming back.

29
00:02:39,926 --> 00:02:47,236
[SPEAKER_01]: So, guard your sense doors, protect the context, don't act out, and do things on the right level, and flies will stop coming.

30
00:02:50,667 --> 00:02:51,628
[SPEAKER_00]: And they can come back.

31
00:02:52,448 --> 00:03:04,197
[SPEAKER_01]: If you lose your behavior, if you start acting, if you start basically accruing again the stench, accumulating the stench, and the flies will come back.

32
00:03:04,217 --> 00:03:05,618
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not something that can be done accidentally.

33
00:03:07,079 --> 00:03:15,605
[SPEAKER_01]: Sure, it can be done carelessly, but because you kept choosing to act out, and go back to desires, and lose your sense restraint, and abandon the context, and give in to distraction, and so on.

34
00:03:16,806 --> 00:03:18,007
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then the flies will come back.

35
00:03:19,598 --> 00:03:35,486
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you're of the view that the flies are the problem and you must be dealing with the flies, you know, through concentrating and this and that and method to stop thinking and all these, like, practices and, you know, whatever people would misunderstand from the suttas, then...

36
00:03:36,878 --> 00:03:40,380
[SPEAKER_01]: You're still not emptying the rubbish because of which the flies are coming.

37
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:42,341
[SPEAKER_01]: You're just chasing the flies more vehemently.

38
00:03:42,501 --> 00:03:44,802
[SPEAKER_00]: You're still... you're putting up these barriers.

39
00:03:45,042 --> 00:03:45,903
[SPEAKER_00]: External barriers.

40
00:03:45,923 --> 00:03:46,023
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure.

41
00:03:46,063 --> 00:03:47,164
[SPEAKER_00]: Nets and... and...

42
00:03:47,184 --> 00:03:48,524
[SPEAKER_00]: Borders, machines.

43
00:03:48,544 --> 00:03:50,365
[SPEAKER_01]: ...traps and repellents.

44
00:03:50,685 --> 00:03:52,106
[SPEAKER_01]: But fundamentally... Yeah.

45
00:03:52,206 --> 00:03:54,568
[SPEAKER_00]: While the very problem is... Yeah.

46
00:03:54,588 --> 00:03:57,249
[SPEAKER_00]: ...the thing that's putting up the borders and the traps and so on.

47
00:03:57,269 --> 00:03:57,529
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

48
00:03:57,549 --> 00:03:58,630
[SPEAKER_00]: That's where the bad smell is.

49
00:03:58,650 --> 00:03:58,830
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

50
00:04:01,608 --> 00:04:12,179
[SPEAKER_01]: So, assuming you can spend the whole life of management, successful to a degree, skilled, with protected circumstances and so on, fundamentally, no, you're still in the same domain.

51
00:04:16,343 --> 00:04:19,986
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you have thoughts of ill-will or thoughts of lust, then, oh, I must get rid of this, this is the problem.

52
00:04:20,006 --> 00:04:20,166
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

53
00:04:20,387 --> 00:04:21,508
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the symptom of the problem.

54
00:04:22,187 --> 00:04:35,353
[SPEAKER_01]: Those thoughts are there because your mind, as said many times, and in the suttas as well, frequently ponders and dwells on things that are attracting lust, lustful thoughts, and angry thoughts, and thoughts of ill-will, and thoughts of distraction.

55
00:04:36,494 --> 00:04:38,495
[SPEAKER_01]: So, don't frequently ponder on those themes.

56
00:04:38,735 --> 00:04:39,255
[SPEAKER_01]: What themes?

57
00:04:39,335 --> 00:04:47,939
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, themes of pleasure is valuable, themes of aversion of pain is justified, themes of these things belong to me and I, you know, I feel entitled to act out and

58
00:04:48,613 --> 00:04:51,734
[SPEAKER_01]: Be free from suffering and get this, and get my jhāna, and get whatever else.

59
00:04:51,754 --> 00:04:52,775
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't want to have to deal with this.

60
00:04:54,115 --> 00:05:00,618
[SPEAKER_01]: The themes of I, the themes of mine, all these themes that are contradictory to the universal nature of experience.

61
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:06,240
[SPEAKER_00]: Those wrong views.

62
00:05:06,260 --> 00:05:06,661
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

63
00:05:06,681 --> 00:05:07,701
[SPEAKER_00]: The dirt.

64
00:05:07,901 --> 00:05:10,082
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, they're perpetuating your attitudes of dirt.

65
00:05:10,222 --> 00:05:12,183
[SPEAKER_01]: The attitudes of longing, the attitude of aversion.

66
00:05:13,463 --> 00:05:14,284
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, that stench.

67
00:05:14,584 --> 00:05:17,045
[SPEAKER_01]: Wanting pleasure, aversion to pain.

68
00:05:19,448 --> 00:05:22,211
[SPEAKER_01]: And everything else comes out of those fundamental cravings.

69
00:05:23,352 --> 00:05:33,180
[SPEAKER_00]: And you can't start the cleansing if you not... if you have that wrong view that it is the world that is making me...

70
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:35,161
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the flies that make me stink.

71
00:05:35,201 --> 00:05:35,962
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

72
00:05:36,603 --> 00:05:36,763
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

73
00:05:37,323 --> 00:05:39,285
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why... That's not where the stanch is.

74
00:05:39,345 --> 00:05:40,966
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the symptom of the stanch.

75
00:05:41,387 --> 00:05:43,068
[SPEAKER_01]: If there are flies, means there is something.

76
00:05:43,108 --> 00:05:43,689
[SPEAKER_01]: And again,

77
00:05:44,419 --> 00:05:46,661
[SPEAKER_01]: Colloquially, flies keep coming back.

78
00:05:46,741 --> 00:05:47,863
[SPEAKER_01]: I'd better check this room.

79
00:05:48,003 --> 00:05:49,204
[SPEAKER_01]: I'd better check this building.

80
00:05:49,424 --> 00:05:51,026
[SPEAKER_01]: It's something they keep coming back for.

81
00:05:52,407 --> 00:05:56,752
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you can't even admit that, you don't have that mundane life.

82
00:05:56,772 --> 00:06:00,876
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, and you wouldn't admit that because it's just too much aversion towards flies.

83
00:06:01,036 --> 00:06:01,677
[SPEAKER_01]: Lustful thoughts.

84
00:06:01,857 --> 00:06:03,859
[SPEAKER_01]: I must get rid of it.

85
00:06:03,879 --> 00:06:04,019
[SPEAKER_01]: Anger.

86
00:06:04,039 --> 00:06:04,680
[SPEAKER_01]: I must get rid of it.

87
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:05,300
[SPEAKER_01]: I must get rid of it.

88
00:06:05,340 --> 00:06:06,561
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where the problem is.

89
00:06:07,510 --> 00:06:10,731
[SPEAKER_01]: And then the idea of what meditation is, it sort of follows out of that.

90
00:06:10,771 --> 00:06:15,392
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, let me just concentrate when I'm not aware of these things anymore, when I stop hearing the flies.

91
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:18,673
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how I'm free from it, you know.

92
00:06:19,333 --> 00:06:21,854
[SPEAKER_00]: That's just how I learn how to concentrate and look away from them.

93
00:06:22,814 --> 00:06:25,735
[SPEAKER_00]: Just, you know, see where the stench is coming from.

94
00:06:27,133 --> 00:06:43,068
[SPEAKER_01]: Accepting that the flies are there because of... Yeah, so not wasting, not perpetuating your views of trying to deal with the flies, but actually focus of, okay, presence of flies means simultaneous presence of the, of the, of the, that which flies are attracted to.

95
00:06:43,228 --> 00:06:47,192
[SPEAKER_01]: So, lustful thoughts cannot become, cannot exist, cannot assail me.

96
00:06:48,328 --> 00:06:52,912
[SPEAKER_01]: I cannot be liable to them unless there is a simultaneously present state of lustful mind.

97
00:06:53,392 --> 00:06:54,753
[SPEAKER_01]: Where is that lustful mind?

98
00:06:55,133 --> 00:06:56,955
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not on the level of the flies and thoughts.

99
00:06:57,255 --> 00:06:59,697
[SPEAKER_01]: It's on the level of signs and features, as we said before.

100
00:07:00,397 --> 00:07:01,958
[SPEAKER_01]: So, how do I discern that?

101
00:07:02,419 --> 00:07:03,259
[SPEAKER_01]: What do I look for?

102
00:07:04,780 --> 00:07:06,201
[SPEAKER_01]: What do I need to do in that sense?

103
00:07:06,321 --> 00:07:16,389
[SPEAKER_01]: But, yeah, if all you do is feel justified about dealing with the flies through all sorts of, you know, management techniques and concentrations and so on,

104
00:07:17,275 --> 00:07:19,377
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, yeah, there's... none of this can apply to you.

105
00:07:20,437 --> 00:07:26,522
[SPEAKER_00]: But that seeing where the problem is, that's close to the right view, you know, that mundane.

106
00:07:26,702 --> 00:07:28,203
[SPEAKER_00]: It's so... it's... Yeah, sure.

107
00:07:28,483 --> 00:07:31,425
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, it's almost... Well, it's kind of necessary for the right view, yeah.

108
00:07:31,925 --> 00:07:36,028
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if you don't even see where the problem is, you won't be able to learn how to do things rightly.

109
00:07:37,109 --> 00:07:40,832
[SPEAKER_01]: For you, endurance would just be, okay, I just have to put up with these flies and do nothing.

110
00:07:41,612 --> 00:07:41,812
[SPEAKER_00]: No?

111
00:07:42,493 --> 00:07:45,395
[SPEAKER_01]: You still got to do something, but it mustn't be aimed at the flies.

112
00:07:47,539 --> 00:07:50,342
[SPEAKER_01]: But all I see is flies and doing something towards flies.

113
00:07:50,382 --> 00:07:50,883
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, exactly.

114
00:07:50,903 --> 00:07:56,368
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you need to learn how else to do something without doing what you take for granted to be done.

115
00:07:56,729 --> 00:07:57,469
[SPEAKER_01]: Deal with the flies.

116
00:07:57,670 --> 00:07:58,691
[SPEAKER_01]: Deal with things that bother me.

117
00:07:59,512 --> 00:08:00,072
[SPEAKER_00]: The middle way.

118
00:08:00,352 --> 00:08:00,533
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

119
00:08:01,313 --> 00:08:07,560
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you're not... if you're going to be trying to deal with things all the time, manage things which are not the actual problem... Yeah.

120
00:08:09,138 --> 00:08:16,744
[SPEAKER_00]: As even if you're doing the the Buddhist so-called... calling your techniques and your management... Yeah, yeah, sure, sure, sure.

121
00:08:17,104 --> 00:08:18,985
[SPEAKER_01]: Verbatim, whatever, do what the Sutta says.

122
00:08:19,005 --> 00:08:19,826
[SPEAKER_01]: You're far from the right thing.

123
00:08:19,846 --> 00:08:21,547
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not doing it on the right level, yeah, yeah.

124
00:08:22,388 --> 00:08:30,674
[SPEAKER_00]: And then in a more... in a very dangerous situation as well, because now you're establishing that for yourself as the way out of suffering.

125
00:08:30,694 --> 00:08:30,794
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

126
00:08:30,814 --> 00:08:31,775
[SPEAKER_00]: When in fact... Yeah.

127
00:08:32,916 --> 00:08:38,560
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not... And then you feel even more justified in managing it and dealing with the flies and preventing flies from coming.

128
00:08:39,352 --> 00:08:45,593
[SPEAKER_01]: Not by removing the bait, but by setting up further traps, and controlling your environment, and avoiding things that disturb you, like the sun.

129
00:08:49,794 --> 00:08:51,655
[SPEAKER_00]: So, how does one get the right view?

130
00:08:53,375 --> 00:08:54,375
[SPEAKER_01]: By not dealing with the flies.

131
00:08:57,316 --> 00:09:01,296
[SPEAKER_00]: Taking this... by reflecting on what... Where the problem is.

132
00:09:01,316 --> 00:09:01,797
[SPEAKER_01]: Where the problem is.

133
00:09:01,817 --> 00:09:02,117
[SPEAKER_01]: What is...

134
00:09:02,717 --> 00:09:08,558
[SPEAKER_01]: Although, you know, everything, all my senses are pointing me, it's because of this, this is why I'm lustful, this is why I'm angry,

135
00:09:09,923 --> 00:09:10,824
[SPEAKER_01]: That's not what the Buddha said.

136
00:09:12,385 --> 00:09:19,590
[SPEAKER_01]: The root of suffering is craving, not the world, not things in the world, not sense objects, not senses, not your thoughts.

137
00:09:21,051 --> 00:09:23,613
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the craving in regard to what is felt.

138
00:09:24,033 --> 00:09:25,114
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's always on me.

139
00:09:25,915 --> 00:09:28,997
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's exactly why the Right View starts with understanding what suffering is.

140
00:09:30,218 --> 00:09:34,661
[SPEAKER_01]: Presence of craving means presence of suffering, not presence of lies or presence of this or that.

141
00:09:34,981 --> 00:09:36,983
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what is that craving that I need to understand?

142
00:09:38,333 --> 00:09:46,196
[SPEAKER_01]: If you... if you discern it, understand it, see its signs and features, that is the right view.

143
00:09:47,436 --> 00:09:50,417
[SPEAKER_01]: You saw the cause of suffering, truly, correctly, accurately.

144
00:09:51,398 --> 00:09:53,418
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, you will know exactly what the escape from it is.

145
00:09:54,599 --> 00:09:58,160
[SPEAKER_01]: You wouldn't need to figure it out as a next step or something.

146
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:00,321
[SPEAKER_01]: Seeing the presence of craving means okay.

147
00:10:00,341 --> 00:10:04,102
[SPEAKER_01]: So, absence of craving means absence of suffering, regardless of the flies and the circumstances.

148
00:10:05,123 --> 00:10:05,543
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what

149
00:10:06,727 --> 00:10:08,708
[SPEAKER_01]: How can I have that craving always absent?

150
00:10:09,048 --> 00:10:10,449
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the Noble Eightfold Path.

151
00:10:10,569 --> 00:10:18,092
[SPEAKER_01]: You may not see it in eight terms, as the Buddha described it, but you would see exactly what that path is in the broad strokes.

152
00:10:18,552 --> 00:10:18,652
[SPEAKER_01]: Ah!

153
00:10:18,952 --> 00:10:27,476
[SPEAKER_01]: Sensory strength, guarding of the sense doors, not acting out, enduring things on the right level until this gratuitous aversion towards discomfort is abandoned, which is craving.

154
00:10:27,997 --> 00:10:31,258
[SPEAKER_01]: Gratuitous aversion towards discomfort that you take for granted is your craving.

155
00:10:32,478 --> 00:10:35,740
[SPEAKER_01]: Gratuitous delight towards comfort is your craving.

156
00:10:35,780 --> 00:10:39,403
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how... there's no a thing, a craving, that you can witness with your senses.

157
00:10:39,503 --> 00:10:46,728
[SPEAKER_01]: It's always the background context that's maintained through careless attitude of pleasure I'm leaning towards.

158
00:10:47,733 --> 00:10:48,714
[SPEAKER_01]: Just just by default.

159
00:10:48,834 --> 00:10:49,274
[SPEAKER_01]: No reason.

160
00:10:49,954 --> 00:10:59,920
[SPEAKER_01]: And the reason is you haven't considered well, thoroughly, frequently, often enough, that leaning towards pleasure is actually dangerous.

161
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:00,920
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the danger.

162
00:11:01,601 --> 00:11:04,462
[SPEAKER_01]: Not presence or absence of pleasure in the world and everything that might happen.

163
00:11:04,482 --> 00:11:04,642
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

164
00:11:04,822 --> 00:11:06,563
[SPEAKER_01]: It's leaning is the trap.

165
00:11:07,184 --> 00:11:09,445
[SPEAKER_01]: Accepting that attitude is how you get trapped.

166
00:11:10,585 --> 00:11:13,987
[SPEAKER_01]: Leaning away from pain, just gratuitously... No.

167
00:11:14,427 --> 00:11:15,148
[SPEAKER_01]: Not wanting it.

168
00:11:16,519 --> 00:11:17,059
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, why?

169
00:11:17,499 --> 00:11:20,060
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, because you never really considered it thoroughly on that level.

170
00:11:24,742 --> 00:11:27,163
[SPEAKER_00]: That leaning towards, that's the longing.

171
00:11:27,203 --> 00:11:28,484
[SPEAKER_01]: Leaning away, that's the aversion.

172
00:11:28,504 --> 00:11:29,144
[SPEAKER_01]: The stench, yeah.

173
00:11:29,184 --> 00:11:30,244
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, that's the stench.

174
00:11:31,165 --> 00:11:33,105
[SPEAKER_00]: And in the suffering, the flies.

175
00:11:33,145 --> 00:11:34,046
[SPEAKER_00]: Flies, the flies.

176
00:11:34,066 --> 00:11:36,927
[SPEAKER_00]: That's all the consequences of it.

177
00:11:37,287 --> 00:11:39,468
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if there is no leaning, there would be no flies.

178
00:11:40,755 --> 00:11:43,416
[SPEAKER_01]: If there is no leaning towards pleasure, there would be no lustful thoughts.

179
00:11:43,916 --> 00:11:46,416
[SPEAKER_01]: If there is no leaning away from pain, i.e.

180
00:11:46,537 --> 00:11:56,299
[SPEAKER_01]: aversion, craving, there would be no angry thoughts, no thoughts of ill-will, no thoughts of discomfort or discontent.

181
00:11:58,780 --> 00:11:59,300
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what I mean.

182
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:03,301
[SPEAKER_01]: Thoughts and hindrances and everything else are the symptoms of the problem.

183
00:12:04,801 --> 00:12:05,702
[SPEAKER_01]: Problem of your craving.

184
00:12:09,057 --> 00:12:12,239
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this is the the verse at the end of that sutta.

185
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:23,205
[SPEAKER_00]: It says, the flies, thoughts based on lust, will run in pursuit of one unrestrained, in the sense faculties, unguarded,

186
00:12:24,377 --> 00:12:30,642
[SPEAKER_00]: A bhikkhu who is polluted, tainted by a stanch, is far from nibbāna, and reaps only distress.

187
00:12:31,543 --> 00:12:40,050
[SPEAKER_00]: Whether in the village or the forest, the unwise, foolish person, not having gained peace for himself, goes around followed by flies.

188
00:12:41,211 --> 00:12:52,039
[SPEAKER_00]: But those accomplished in virtuous behavior, who delight in wisdom and peace, those peaceful ones live happily, having destroyed the flies.

189
00:12:54,383 --> 00:12:57,076
[SPEAKER_00]: Having destroyed them, having starved them away.

